\f2\i \cf2 What the tax?
\f1\i0  While Gerry\'92s mind failed to catch up, his body obeyed. The PAPER agent stayed standing, always behind, always watching. The other figure crumpled into a visitor\'92s chair and presented his teeth. Gerry guessed it was a smile. He\'92d never seen such a thing in all the broadcasts as this man trying to smile. Gerry was unsure whether the smile\'92s intent was for reassurance or for inducing terror.\
Piotr Dunhilton, CEO of Ulyssia. On broadcasts, they called him \'93salamander face\'94\'97though, on seeing him up close, Gerry decided that was terribly unfair to most salamanders. His complexion was soft as undercooked tofu and had the general sheen of a wet rock after rain. Above the pale, waxy cheeks were God\'92s little afterthoughts: eyes set too far apart; a nose more suggestion than feature; and a smile of uniform chalky teeth, delimited by lips so flat and pink they could have been painted on by a distracted apprentice.\
\'93I understand they call you Very Hard Man in these halls,\'94 the CEO said, now thankfully not attempting a smile.\
\'93I, ah, prefer Gerry, your Serene Corporateness.\'94\
\'93Oh?\'94 said Dunhilton, all pantomime. \'93Well, I am informed\'94\'97he flicked a glance at the PAPER agent\'97\'93you, Gerry, are exactly what we need in these troubled times.\'94\
\'93Sir?\'94\
\'93The previous Commissioner has, shall we say, unexpectedly retired.\'94\
\'93I thought he was on holiday,\'94 Gerry blurted.\
\'93Well, retirement is the most final of holidays,\'94 the CEO replied.\
Gerry nodded. \'93I imagine, perhaps, he retired out a window?\'94\
\'93Ah, no,\'94 Dunhilton deflected. \'93Someone wanted to send us a much stronger message.\'94\
What could be stronger than a window retirement, idiomatically called a pillowing? The Layer would strip you as you fell, then you\'92d hit the ground. A brief, final transfer to Cloudborne living; for some, their only trip below the Layer.\
The CEO stood; Gerry copied him, automatically. The CEO offered his hand. Gerry, on reflex, accepted.\
\'93Congratulations. Special Agent Jones will read you in. Good day.\'94\
The CEO left while Gerry was still mid-stammer. Agent Jones, stone-faced, straightened his black tie, and ground his teeth.
